{% comment %}
  Nourishment explorer: for each nourished stretch, the yearly satellite shoreline on the stretch and on the rest of
  the island (or their difference), with each fill's jump and what was left in the last full year. Observed only.
  Data from tools/hatteras_nourishment_data.py; script assets/hatteras/js/nourishment-explorer.js.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="hat-mvo hat-nx hat-bleed" data-src="{{ '/assets/hatteras/data/nourishment.json' | relative_url }}">
  <div class="hat-shoremap-inner">
    <div class="hat-controls">
      <div class="hat-seg hat-nx-stretches" role="group" aria-label="Nourished stretch"></div>
      <div class="hat-seg hat-nx-views" role="group" aria-label="What to show">
        <button type="button" data-view="relative" class="on">Relative to the rest of the island</button>
        <button type="button" data-view="raw">Shoreline position</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hat-nx-strip" aria-hidden="false"></div>
    <div class="hat-tl-chart hat-nx-chart" role="img" aria-label="Shoreline position through time on the chosen nourished stretch"></div>
    <div class="hat-tl-tip" role="status" hidden></div>
    <div class="hat-nx-cards"></div>
    <p class="hat-caption hat-numbered" data-for-view="relative">
      How far the shoreline on the nourished stretch moved compared with the rest of the island, from the yearly average of
      every satellite shoreline. Both are set to zero in the year before the first fill (open circle). Storms and island-wide
      shifts such as 2021 move both, so they cancel here and a fill shows up as a jump; the gold bracket is the change from the
      year before the fill to the year after. Before any fill, a falling line means the stretch was eroding faster than
      the island as a whole. Gold bands mark fill years.
    </p>
    <p class="hat-caption hat-numbered" data-for-view="raw" hidden>
      The yearly average shoreline on the nourished stretch (blue) and on the rest of the island from Cape Point to Oregon Inlet (grey),
      both set to zero in the year before the first fill (open circle). The gap between the two lines is the
      "relative to the rest of the island" view. Gold bands mark fill years.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/hatteras/js/nourishment-explorer.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
